 "preferred_name": "File control block",
 "kind": "knowledge",
 "definition": "A data structure in an operating system or file system that holds the information needed to manage an open file.",
 "description": {
  "text": "A file system structure that holds the state of an open file. The operating system manages it but it sits in the memory of the program using the file, so a process can keep as many files open as it has memory for. It originates from CP/M and appears in most DOS variants.",
